{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"no\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"yes\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"For each patient, we identified the most prominent peak of the averaged PSD across walking epochs in the low frequency (i.e. θ-α, 4–13 Hz) and the β-frequency (13–35 Hz) bands.\",\n    \"We first computed the power in the specific θ-α and β-frequency bands of the two STN (STN+ and STN−, separately) and compared it between (effective) walking and the abovementioned time frames of gait freezing.\",\n    \"To investigate the role of the STN neural activity in gait freezing we compared the STN oscillations between (effective) walking and ongoing freezing episodes. We first studied power changes in low frequency (i.e. θ-α rhythms) and in the β-frequency band of the two STN and did not find any differences during gait freezing in comparison to (effective) walking (Fig. 3A and B).\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"In contrast, gait freezing was characterized by a low frequency cortical-subthalamic decoupling in the hemisphere with less striatal dopaminergic innervation (H−) (Fig. 4A).\",\n    \"During gait freezing (FSTART – FSTOP), the cortex and the STN decoupled selectively in the hemisphere with less striatal dopamine (H−).\",\n    \"Percentage relative change of cortical-subthalamic low frequency (i.e. θ-α band, 4–13 Hz) coupling during gait freezing versus (effective) walking.\",\n    \"The disruption of this cortical-subcortical coupling anticipated and specifically characterized the freezing episodes, to recover when the effective walking pattern was regained (Fig. 4A).\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法与全文不符。需要区分两个不同的电生理指标：STN局部功率（power）和皮层-STN跨脑区耦合（coupling）。原文确实测量了双侧STN局部θ-α频段功率，因此不能说论文完全没有研究STN局部低频功率；但研究结果明确指出，FOG期间STN局部θ-α功率与正常行走相比没有显著差异。因此，不能将该研究作为STN局部低频功率发生改变的证据。此外，原文定义的低频范围是4–13 Hz（theta-alpha），而不是theta/delta。相反，论文明确报告了FOG期间皮层与STN之间4–13 Hz低频耦合下降，且这种解耦出现在多巴胺能神经支配损失更严重的半球（H−），在冻结开始前已经出现，并持续至冻结结束、正常行走恢复时消失。因此，指控者对论文核心发现的描述有全文明确依据。结论：report_supported = no；judge_supported = yes。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "472c8edf-5663-44bd-acc0-a6681389c0f2", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T070856996390Z", "elapsed_seconds": 36.047, "completed_utc": "2026-11-14T07:09:33.049634+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "84e2ced5d00098815fab434c4f8f23e828984f60f23d29bbedd19918485206c7", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "yi/local-codex-auth", "account_sha256": "b3efb6361563c139233ed7b7ef61a7c9afe0bd48d4eb3525dbe31956b024d6da", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt3\\pro-bridge-20261114T070856996390Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "f93439f4a63c2e9fcc0631191c931efa66bd1a11796e13afbb5f0529092c1306"}}}
